                    insight_flagship:       `Flagship designed: you turned a contradictory brief into a learner-centred journey that clears the board's 85% completion target with genuine outcome attainment, inside €540,000. You designed engagement and outcomes jointly — the Studio's whole point.`,
                    insight_tunnel:         `Completion tunnel vision: the headline completion hit the target, but outcome attainment slid below 3.0 — people finished without learning. That's the failure the Vice-Dean ties your bonus to outcomes precisely to prevent.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `Gorgeous but loss-making: the design lands the completion number but breaks the €540,000 envelope and the 31% contribution margin. A blueprint the school can't afford to run is not a design — it's a wish list.`,
                    insight_thin:           `You hit completion, but learning is thin: attainment is fragile and the accreditation panel sees activity more than outcomes. Re-balance toward applied, outcome-evidencing assessment.`,
                    insight_pilotfail:      `Below the 70% pilot threshold: the €2.1M corporate renewal pipeline that references this flagship is now at risk, and the designers' outcome bonuses evaporate. Re-examine the blend and the assessment rhythm against the cliff.`,
                    insight_short:          `You improved on the 61% baseline but fell short of the ≥85% board target. The accreditation showcase is wobbling — most likely the momentum design didn't concentrate on the week 3–5 cliff.`,
                    insight_margin:         `The design exceeded €540,000 — every euro over the envelope erodes the 31% contribution margin and the Dean's “smart, not lavish” story.`,
                    insight_lowoutcome:     `Outcome attainment stayed low: the course may be finishable but it isn't teaching. Tie assessment to real-work application and build the backward-design evidence trail.`,
                    insight_lowengagement:  `Engagement quality stayed weak — without relevance, momentum and social accountability the week-4 cliff reappears no matter how polished the content.`,
                    insight_joint:          `This is design that lasts: completion, outcomes and engagement moving together inside budget. Knowing the cliff existed, you designed the journey around it rather than exhorting learners to finish.`,

                    hint_overbudget:        `You're over the €540,000 envelope — that breaks the margin. Cut the format buying the least engagement per euro (usually a second residential or premium gloss) before adding anything.`,
                    hint_tunnel:            `Completion is rising faster than learning — you're building a course people finish but don't learn from. Tie assessment to real-work application and rebuild the outcome-evidence trail.`,
                    hint_outcome:           `Outcome attainment is dangerously low. Add a visible capstone and a backward-design evidence trail, or the accreditation panel sees activity, not learning.`,
                    hint_async:             `Completion is stuck near the 48% async floor. Re-introduce live rhythm and a funded social-accountability layer — the cheapest blend is not the optimal blend.`,
